1
00:00:03,520 --> 00:00:07,160
♪By red walls and a dry well,
my crown gathers dust and frost♪

2
00:00:07,720 --> 00:00:11,840
♪With a hoe and a patch of wasteland,
I sow the moonlight♪

3
00:00:12,160 --> 00:00:16,160
♪Who says the Cold Palace
holds nothing but tears?♪

4
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:20,440
♪I choose to fill it with fragrant wine♪

5
00:00:20,640 --> 00:00:22,200
♪Farming in the Cold Palace♪

6
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:24,360
♪Growing life's simple joys♪

7
00:00:24,680 --> 00:00:26,800
♪Bins full of grain, jars full of wine♪

8
00:00:27,080 --> 00:00:28,800
♪Better than dancing in silks♪

9
00:00:29,360 --> 00:00:30,680
♪Farming in the Cold Palace♪

10
00:00:30,880 --> 00:00:33,360
♪My heart longs for the world beyond♪

11
00:00:33,880 --> 00:00:35,840
♪Tending a courtyard full of life♪

12
00:00:36,120 --> 00:00:40,640
♪Come, share a cup with me♪

13
00:00:40,640 --> 00:00:42,600
(Welcome to Cold Palace Refreshments)

14
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:46,480
=Farm Busily in the Cold Palace=

15
00:00:46,680 --> 00:00:48,680
(Based on Hongshu.com's novel
I'm Busy Farming in the Cold Palace)

16
00:00:48,680 --> 00:00:49,680
=Episode 12=

17
00:00:52,280 --> 00:00:53,280
Triple?

18
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:54,719
He might as well kill me!

19
00:00:54,759 --> 00:00:55,880
His Majesty says

20
00:00:56,280 --> 00:00:57,399
if it's too much,

21
00:00:57,719 --> 00:00:59,439
you can go bargain with him.

22
00:00:59,759 --> 00:01:01,079
(Does he think I'm stupid?)

23
00:01:01,079 --> 00:01:02,240
(If I go,)

24
00:01:02,479 --> 00:01:04,239
(even the 10,000 taels I got from
Consort Yao)

25
00:01:04,239 --> 00:01:05,159
(I'd have to give it back.)

26
00:01:09,439 --> 00:01:10,480
Triple it is.

27
00:01:11,239 --> 00:01:11,879
Yinshuang.

28
00:01:12,120 --> 00:01:13,120
Bring the money.

29
00:01:13,640 --> 00:01:14,439
What?

30
00:01:14,920 --> 00:01:15,519
But...

31
00:01:15,519 --> 00:01:16,040
You...

32
00:01:16,120 --> 00:01:17,280
You're giving in already?

33
00:01:17,680 --> 00:01:19,239
(At least put up a fight!)

34
00:01:20,319 --> 00:01:22,760
Defying him would cost me my head.

35
00:01:24,840 --> 00:01:27,799
His Majesty just wants you to back down.

36
00:01:27,799 --> 00:01:28,760
Back down?

37
00:01:29,439 --> 00:01:31,280
Not in this lifetime.

38
00:01:33,319 --> 00:01:34,400
(Within three days,)

39
00:01:34,439 --> 00:01:36,879
(he'll beg to pay it all back,
with interest.)

40
00:01:43,680 --> 00:01:44,599
My lady.

41
00:01:44,840 --> 00:01:47,400
These seed heads are rock hard.

42
00:01:47,599 --> 00:01:48,920
Can we really eat them?

43
00:01:53,599 --> 00:01:54,319
Try it.

44
00:02:08,680 --> 00:02:09,680
So sweet!

45
00:02:09,879 --> 00:02:10,879
Delicious.

46
00:02:11,919 --> 00:02:13,680
(In my Virtual Farm,)

47
00:02:13,680 --> 00:02:15,879
(I carefully bred this super wheat.)

48
00:02:15,879 --> 00:02:18,120
(It yields more and tastes better.)

49
00:02:18,199 --> 00:02:19,800
(It grows best in dry soil.)

50
00:02:21,199 --> 00:02:23,039
While gathering herbs last month,

51
00:02:23,199 --> 00:02:25,000
I discovered this new wheat variety.

52
00:02:25,199 --> 00:02:27,360
It grew even better after replanting.

53
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:28,159
With this,

54
00:02:28,319 --> 00:02:30,400
Donglan will never face famine again.

55
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:30,800
Mm.

56
00:02:31,800 --> 00:02:34,639
Your Majesty!

57
00:02:34,879 --> 00:02:35,759
Come and see!

58
00:02:35,759 --> 00:02:37,199
Our cucumbers are gone!

59
00:02:37,560 --> 00:02:38,360
Cucumbers?

60
00:02:38,639 --> 00:02:39,479
What cucumbers?

61
00:02:39,680 --> 00:02:40,840
I never planted any.

62
00:02:41,039 --> 00:02:43,039
I'm sure we planted cucumbers.

63
00:02:43,199 --> 00:02:45,439
I even picked two in secret.

64
00:02:45,439 --> 00:02:46,680
You must be mistaken.

65
00:02:47,840 --> 00:02:48,919
Go get ready.

66
00:02:48,919 --> 00:02:50,680
We have to harvest all the wheat today.

67
00:02:52,080 --> 00:02:52,840
Yes, Your Majesty.

68
00:02:54,439 --> 00:02:56,000
Brother, time to work!

69
00:02:56,080 --> 00:02:56,879
Coming!

70
00:03:00,599 --> 00:03:01,400
Look, Your Majesty.

71
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:02,879
He's holding a cucumber!

72
00:03:03,080 --> 00:03:04,719
You're the cucumber!

73
00:03:04,719 --> 00:03:05,960
Less talk, more work.

74
00:03:07,919 --> 00:03:08,680
Come on.

75
00:03:11,599 --> 00:03:12,599
Ta-da!

76
00:03:14,039 --> 00:03:14,680
You,

77
00:03:14,680 --> 00:03:15,560
dry the grain first.

78
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:16,199
You,

79
00:03:16,360 --> 00:03:17,319
thresh in the stone mortar.

80
00:03:17,520 --> 00:03:18,319
You, sift the bran.

81
00:03:18,680 --> 00:03:19,439
Let's get started!

82
00:03:28,479 --> 00:03:29,599
Keep it moving!

83
00:03:30,199 --> 00:03:31,120
That's it!

84
00:03:37,960 --> 00:03:40,599
(Once he sees my plump steamed buns...)

85
00:03:41,199 --> 00:03:42,199
I'll win him over.

86
00:03:59,400 --> 00:04:05,400
(Liu's Grain Route Is Open
The Convoy Departs in Three Days)

87
00:04:15,960 --> 00:04:17,000
Liu's grain route is open.

88
00:04:17,279 --> 00:04:19,519
The convoy leaves in three days.

89
00:04:20,639 --> 00:04:21,959
If anything goes wrong again...

90
00:04:23,199 --> 00:04:25,720
I stake my life on it, Your Majesty.

91
00:04:27,319 --> 00:04:28,120
Your Majesty.

92
00:04:28,360 --> 00:04:29,639
Her Majesty seeks an audience.

93
00:04:30,360 --> 00:04:31,279
Which one?

94
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:34,120
From the Cold Palace.

95
00:04:37,560 --> 00:04:39,199
Didn't she refuse to yield?

96
00:04:39,360 --> 00:04:40,879
Changed her mind overnight?

97
00:04:41,199 --> 00:04:43,000
If she wants her silver back,

98
00:04:43,240 --> 00:04:44,279
she can forget it.

99
00:04:44,800 --> 00:04:46,720
You're still upset, Your Majesty.

100
00:04:46,800 --> 00:04:48,160
We have company.

101
00:04:48,439 --> 00:04:49,240
Send her in.

102
00:04:50,519 --> 00:04:53,519
Her Majesty may enter!

103
00:04:54,600 --> 00:04:55,879
(Let's see)

104
00:04:56,120 --> 00:04:57,879
(what game she's playing this time.)

105
00:05:04,399 --> 00:05:05,759
This is the wheat I told you about.

106
00:05:06,160 --> 00:05:07,199
The grain is ground into flour,

107
00:05:07,199 --> 00:05:08,399
then fermented and steamed.

108
00:05:08,560 --> 00:05:10,959
It tastes good and keeps you full.

109
00:05:12,360 --> 00:05:13,360
What's the yield per mu?

110
00:05:14,399 --> 00:05:15,199
10 shi.

111
00:05:18,399 --> 00:05:19,279
How many harvests a year?

112
00:05:19,759 --> 00:05:20,600
Three on dry land.

113
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:22,800
Perfect for Donglan's climate.

114
00:05:38,759 --> 00:05:39,600
Is it good?

115
00:05:49,120 --> 00:05:49,839
Eunuch Cao.

116
00:05:51,279 --> 00:05:52,519
One for me too?

117
00:05:53,839 --> 00:05:54,879
Thank you, Your Majesty.

118
00:05:57,199 --> 00:05:58,279
(When the relief grain rotted,)

119
00:05:58,279 --> 00:05:59,439
(he offered his life.)

120
00:05:59,439 --> 00:06:00,600
(That takes courage.)

121
00:06:01,839 --> 00:06:03,480
Try one, my lord.

122
00:06:07,079 --> 00:06:08,399
Go on, take it.

123
00:06:09,240 --> 00:06:10,120
Thank you.

124
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:12,800
The bun is soft as a cloud,

125
00:06:12,800 --> 00:06:14,560
with rich broth inside.

126
00:06:14,680 --> 00:06:17,639
I've never had a staple this good!

127
00:06:19,079 --> 00:06:20,560
If all this is true,

128
00:06:20,800 --> 00:06:23,120
Donglan need never know hunger again.

129
00:06:23,959 --> 00:06:25,040
If I may,

130
00:06:25,199 --> 00:06:27,040
for tens of thousands in Donglan,

131
00:06:27,279 --> 00:06:29,199
thank Your Majesty for this blessing.

132
00:06:29,839 --> 00:06:30,839
Please, don't!

133
00:06:30,839 --> 00:06:32,639
You're old enough to be my father.

134
00:06:32,639 --> 00:06:34,160
Don't bow to me like that!

135
00:06:34,480 --> 00:06:35,560
I wouldn't dare presume.

136
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:39,720
Cao Zhongquan.

137
00:06:41,160 --> 00:06:42,360
Summon the Agriculture Minister

138
00:06:42,639 --> 00:06:43,720
at once.

139
00:06:43,759 --> 00:06:44,639
Yes, Your Majesty.

140
00:06:50,680 --> 00:06:53,279
(Surely that makes up for my mistakes.)

141
00:07:00,120 --> 00:07:01,639
I've searched the ancient records.

142
00:07:01,639 --> 00:07:04,160
No crop in the records yields this much.

143
00:07:04,519 --> 00:07:05,800
Heaven blesses Donglan!

144
00:07:05,879 --> 00:07:08,439
This is a gift from above!

145
00:07:09,120 --> 00:07:10,560
Such plump grains,

146
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:12,519
such fine flour.

147
00:07:12,560 --> 00:07:14,000
Exceptional quality.

148
00:07:14,879 --> 00:07:17,120
But we've never grown it before.

149
00:07:17,439 --> 00:07:18,800
We have only 2 dou of wheat seed.

150
00:07:19,199 --> 00:07:21,079
What if the trial fails?

151
00:07:22,839 --> 00:07:23,639
Your Majesty,

152
00:07:24,279 --> 00:07:27,199
the Empress grew this wheat herself.

153
00:07:27,360 --> 00:07:29,160
Why not let her lead the trial?

154
00:07:29,399 --> 00:07:31,920
She grew it in the Cold Palace.

155
00:07:31,920 --> 00:07:33,439
She must understand it well.

156
00:07:33,680 --> 00:07:34,600
Absurd!

157
00:07:34,839 --> 00:07:36,439
Farming is the foundation of our realm.

158
00:07:36,560 --> 00:07:37,879
How can we entrust it

159
00:07:37,879 --> 00:07:40,079
to a disgraced woman in the Cold Palace?

160
00:07:40,279 --> 00:07:41,519
What if she fails?

161
00:07:42,399 --> 00:07:44,240
Why so worked up, Director Zhao?

162
00:07:44,319 --> 00:07:46,439
Afraid a good harvest

163
00:07:46,519 --> 00:07:47,879
will make the Imperial Observatory's

164
00:07:47,920 --> 00:07:50,439
stargazing and divination look useless?

165
00:07:50,839 --> 00:07:54,160
Can any son of yours tell grains apart?

166
00:07:54,160 --> 00:07:54,839
You!

167
00:07:56,839 --> 00:07:57,959
Oh, I forgot.

168
00:07:57,959 --> 00:07:59,959
You have no sons.

169
00:08:00,639 --> 00:08:01,680
Have you perhaps

170
00:08:01,920 --> 00:08:04,160
revealed too many of heaven's secrets?

171
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:07,839
I've never had a grudge against you.

172
00:08:07,839 --> 00:08:09,920
Why insult me?

173
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:12,759
Had the Imperial Observatory
foreseen the storm,

174
00:08:13,079 --> 00:08:14,920
our grain reserves wouldn't have rotted!

175
00:08:14,920 --> 00:08:16,360
A full 50,000 shi!

176
00:08:16,680 --> 00:08:17,959
How many lives could that have saved?

177
00:08:18,560 --> 00:08:19,560
Every day I...

178
00:08:19,560 --> 00:08:20,079
I...

179
00:08:20,079 --> 00:08:20,800
Enough.

180
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:23,160
My decision is made.

181
00:08:23,240 --> 00:08:24,000
Cao Zhongquan.

182
00:08:24,199 --> 00:08:24,920
Here, Your Majesty.

183
00:08:24,920 --> 00:08:26,040
Read the decree.

184
00:08:26,040 --> 00:08:26,759
Yes, Your Majesty.

185
00:08:30,879 --> 00:08:32,159
By the Mandate of Heaven,

186
00:08:32,159 --> 00:08:33,639
His Majesty decrees:

187
00:08:33,639 --> 00:08:36,120
for her service in cultivating wheat,

188
00:08:36,120 --> 00:08:37,960
Lady Lu shall leave the Cold Palace

189
00:08:37,960 --> 00:08:40,440
and reside in Fengming Palace.

190
00:08:40,440 --> 00:08:42,720
She is granted 100 mu of imperial land

191
00:08:42,720 --> 00:08:44,000
and sixty workers.

192
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:46,120
Agriculture Office staff and supplies

193
00:08:46,120 --> 00:08:47,519
shall be at her disposal.

194
00:08:47,840 --> 00:08:48,799
If the harvest succeeds,

195
00:08:48,799 --> 00:08:50,240
(Imperial Decree)
She gets first credit.

196
00:08:50,240 --> 00:08:51,639
Thus decreed.

197
00:08:52,360 --> 00:08:53,159
Your Majesty.

198
00:08:53,639 --> 00:08:56,879
His Majesty sent me
to escort you from the Cold Palace.

199
00:08:57,639 --> 00:08:58,919
Heaven has shown mercy!

200
00:08:59,320 --> 00:09:01,320
Your hard days are finally over.

201
00:09:01,320 --> 00:09:02,360
Congratulations, my lady!

202
00:09:02,720 --> 00:09:03,600
Mind your manners.

203
00:09:03,600 --> 00:09:04,759
Still calling her 'my lady'?

204
00:09:10,279 --> 00:09:11,200
I'm not going anywhere.

205
00:09:11,279 --> 00:09:12,440
I'm staying right here.

206
00:09:14,200 --> 00:09:15,919
Why, Your Majesty?

207
00:09:16,039 --> 00:09:18,320
Fengming Palace housed every empress.

208
00:09:18,519 --> 00:09:21,039
His Majesty is clearly honoring you.

209
00:09:21,639 --> 00:09:22,960
(Who wants that honor?)

210
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:24,879
(It doesn't sound fit for the living.)

211
00:09:25,759 --> 00:09:27,200
I'm used to hard times.

212
00:09:27,360 --> 00:09:29,080
A fine life isn't for me.

213
00:09:29,919 --> 00:09:31,679
(Where else could I be this free?)

214
00:09:31,799 --> 00:09:33,440
(How could I run my shops if I left?)

215
00:09:33,639 --> 00:09:35,960
(Turn Fengming Palace into
the Empress's Wonder Shop?)

216
00:09:35,960 --> 00:09:37,080
(Who would dare shop there?)

217
00:09:40,679 --> 00:09:42,080
(Cold Palace)
Greetings, Your Majesty.

218
00:09:43,679 --> 00:09:45,360
You crafty wild boar.

219
00:09:46,320 --> 00:09:48,399
So you're determined to stay here?

220
00:09:57,240 --> 00:09:58,559
Will you walk,

221
00:09:59,120 --> 00:10:00,639
or do I have to carry you out?

222
00:10:01,440 --> 00:10:02,679
(Carry me out?)

223
00:10:03,519 --> 00:10:05,120
Then I'd really be a wild boar!

224
00:10:20,360 --> 00:10:21,080
Ji Wujue!

225
00:10:21,519 --> 00:10:22,679
Have you lost your mind?

226
00:10:22,840 --> 00:10:24,360
I defied the Empress Dowager

227
00:10:24,840 --> 00:10:26,600
and overruled the court to restore you.

228
00:10:26,759 --> 00:10:27,960
Why defy my decree?

229
00:10:28,399 --> 00:10:29,600
Who asked to be restored?

230
00:10:29,919 --> 00:10:31,120
I want freedom!

231
00:10:32,960 --> 00:10:35,039
From the start, you've been my Empress.

232
00:10:35,480 --> 00:10:37,559
And from the start,
I've been in the Cold Palace.

233
00:10:39,399 --> 00:10:40,559
Your family had fallen.

234
00:10:41,679 --> 00:10:43,600
With no clan to support you,

235
00:10:44,279 --> 00:10:45,600
you'd be everyone's target.

236
00:10:47,080 --> 00:10:47,879
What about now?

237
00:10:48,639 --> 00:10:51,759
Are you making me a target again?

238
00:10:53,480 --> 00:10:54,759
You foresee the future,

239
00:10:55,440 --> 00:10:56,440
plan far ahead,

240
00:10:57,279 --> 00:10:58,440
and seem to know everything.

241
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:00,559
So I deserve to be trapped,

242
00:11:00,600 --> 00:11:03,399
sacrificed as a pawn
for your royal family?

243
00:11:04,559 --> 00:11:05,639
If you keep pushing me,

244
00:11:06,200 --> 00:11:07,519
I won't grow the wheat!

245
00:11:12,559 --> 00:11:14,639
Fine. Don't grow it.

246
00:11:16,279 --> 00:11:17,559
Bear me an heir instead.

247
00:11:26,240 --> 00:11:27,879
I can restore you as Empress

248
00:11:28,600 --> 00:11:30,399
or pin you beneath me in bed.

249
00:11:55,120 --> 00:11:56,879
Mother says my harem is too empty

250
00:11:57,720 --> 00:11:58,799
and makes me choose consorts.

251
00:12:00,360 --> 00:12:03,440
Ministers accuse me of defying propriety
and ruling the court as I please.

252
00:12:04,240 --> 00:12:07,399
The Censorate's memorials
burned for two whole hours.

253
00:12:10,320 --> 00:12:13,039
I only want the woman I love by my side.

254
00:12:15,360 --> 00:12:16,519
Is that so wrong?

255
00:12:20,320 --> 00:12:22,279
But I don't want to be bound

256
00:12:23,039 --> 00:12:23,840
by rigid moral codes.

257
00:12:25,320 --> 00:12:28,240
or compete with all your other consorts.

258
00:12:30,440 --> 00:12:31,559
I'll exempt you from those rules.

259
00:12:32,399 --> 00:12:33,879
I'll have no other consorts.

260
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:36,320
Whatever you want,

261
00:12:37,720 --> 00:12:38,960
I can give it to you.

262
00:12:41,519 --> 00:12:42,720
Born into royalty,

263
00:12:44,120 --> 00:12:45,120
what in your life

264
00:12:46,039 --> 00:12:47,799
can you truly decide for yourself?

265
00:12:52,399 --> 00:12:54,399
Mother.

266
00:12:56,679 --> 00:12:57,799
Don't cry.

267
00:12:57,960 --> 00:12:59,440
(Empress Rui, Ji Wujue's Mother)
Silly boy.

268
00:13:00,759 --> 00:13:02,360
Your tears are too heavy.

269
00:13:03,240 --> 00:13:04,279
Mother...

270
00:13:04,480 --> 00:13:05,799
I can't take them with me.

271
00:13:07,720 --> 00:13:08,759
Look.

272
00:13:09,399 --> 00:13:10,960
The wind is here.

273
00:13:12,159 --> 00:13:15,720
At last, I can see the world outside.

274
00:13:16,120 --> 00:13:17,799
If you leave me, Mother,

275
00:13:17,919 --> 00:13:19,759
what will I do?

276
00:13:20,519 --> 00:13:24,879
I'll be the willow fluff in spring,

277
00:13:25,200 --> 00:13:27,039
and fireflies on summer nights.

278
00:13:28,039 --> 00:13:30,039
When you miss me, Jue,

279
00:13:30,879 --> 00:13:32,279
just open your window.

280
00:13:33,399 --> 00:13:36,240
I shouldn't have borne you into royalty.

281
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:38,440
Jue,

282
00:13:38,879 --> 00:13:39,759
you should

283
00:13:40,480 --> 00:13:41,559
be free,

284
00:13:42,440 --> 00:13:43,639
to live as you please.

285
00:13:46,960 --> 00:13:48,879
Mother!

286
00:13:49,320 --> 00:13:52,159
Mother!

287
00:14:14,960 --> 00:14:15,759
All right.

288
00:14:17,519 --> 00:14:18,759
Then you don't have to.

289
00:14:20,360 --> 00:14:21,519
I'll do as you wish.

290
00:14:58,600 --> 00:15:02,320
♪By red walls and a dry well,
my crown gathers dust and frost♪

291
00:15:02,760 --> 00:15:07,000
♪With a hoe and a patch of wasteland,
I sow the moonlight♪

292
00:15:07,280 --> 00:15:11,320
♪Who says the Cold Palace
holds nothing but tears?♪

293
00:15:11,600 --> 00:15:15,760
♪I choose to fill it with fragrant wine♪

294
00:15:16,160 --> 00:15:19,960
♪Cool dew, starry nights,
wheat sprouts in my hands♪

295
00:15:20,240 --> 00:15:24,360
♪I shape fields, not painted brows,
and fill them with hope♪

296
00:15:24,880 --> 00:15:28,160
♪Gold and silver bloom from the soil♪

297
00:15:28,640 --> 00:15:33,320
♪I smile as the world storms on♪

298
00:15:35,360 --> 00:15:37,120
♪No finery to rival spring♪

299
00:15:37,520 --> 00:15:41,600
♪All I wish for are waves of green♪

300
00:15:44,080 --> 00:15:45,720
♪Where is beauty found?♪

301
00:15:45,880 --> 00:15:50,440
♪Just lift your eyes and see♪

302
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:52,480
♪Farming in the Cold Palace♪

303
00:15:52,720 --> 00:15:54,640
♪Growing life's simple joys♪

304
00:15:55,040 --> 00:15:57,080
♪Bins full of grain, jars full of wine♪

305
00:15:57,400 --> 00:15:59,080
♪Better than dancing in silks♪

306
00:15:59,640 --> 00:16:00,960
♪Farming in the Cold Palace♪

307
00:16:01,280 --> 00:16:03,640
♪My heart longs for the world beyond♪

308
00:16:04,120 --> 00:16:06,120
♪Tending a courtyard full of life♪

309
00:16:06,480 --> 00:16:10,480
♪Come, share a cup with me♪
